{{!
	string msg-arknights-drawer-toggle / msg-toc
	string msg-arknights-nav-screen
	object data-search-box   core search box data
	object data-reading-prefs  href (Special:ReadingPreferences, with returnto) / msg-label / data-form
	bool toc-enabled
	object data-user-menu

	The header carries no site navigation: that lives in the sidebar only (MediaWiki:MenuSidebar
	or the MediaWiki:Sidebar portlets), which is reachable at every width — as a column at ≥ 1120px
	and as the drawer opened from the local nav's menu button.
}}
<header class="ak-header mw-header" id="mw-head">
	<div class="ak-header__inner">
		{{>Header__logo}}
		{{#data-search-box}}{{>Search}}{{/data-search-box}}
		{{!
			Phones (< 640): search collapses to this icon, which opens the palette.
			With the palette off, search.js falls back to revealing #searchform in place —
			hence both aria-haspopup and the aria-controls/-expanded pair.
		}}
		<button type="button" class="ak-btn ak-btn--icon ak-header__search-toggle ak-only-mobile" id="ak-search-toggle" aria-label="{{msg-arknights-search-toggle}}" title="{{msg-arknights-search-toggle}}" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="searchform" aria-expanded="false">
			<span class="ak-icon ak-icon--search"></span>
		</button>
		{{!
			Below 1120px the tools (reading preferences, notifications, user menu) collapse into the
			card pulled down by the burger; above it .ak-header__screen is display:contents, so they
			take part in the main row's grid directly. One DOM either way — the Echo and #p-personal
			ids are never duplicated.

			Opening the card is pure CSS, so it works without JS: the checkbox has to precede both
			the card and the label for `~` to reach them. header.js only adds Escape, outside
			clicks and closing again on the way back to desktop widths.
		}}
		<input type="checkbox" id="ak-nav-toggle" class="ak-nav-cb" aria-controls="ak-nav-screen">
		<div class="ak-header__screen" id="ak-nav-screen">
			<div class="ak-header__tools">
				{{!
					Reading preferences (appearance, sections, text size — Vector 2022's "Appearance"
					menu): glasses, left of the bell. A link to the special page, which is what it
					stays without JS; client-prefs.js opens the panel below instead.
				}}
				{{#data-reading-prefs}}
				<a class="ak-btn ak-btn--icon ak-header__prefs" id="ak-prefs-toggle" href="{{href}}" title="{{msg-label}}" aria-label="{{msg-label}}" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="ak-prefs-panel" aria-expanded="false"><svg class="ak-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-glasses"/></svg></a>
				{{/data-reading-prefs}}
				{{#data-user-menu}}{{>UserMenu}}{{/data-user-menu}}
			</div>
		</div>
		<label class="ak-header__burger" for="ak-nav-toggle">
			<span class="ak-header__burger-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
			<span class="ak-sr-only">{{msg-arknights-nav-screen}}</span>
		</label>
	</div>
	{{!
		Local nav — the drawer button, shown by CSS below 1120px only, and on phones (≤ 639px)
		the table-of-contents button. It is no row of its own: CSS folds both into the header's
		single row (display:contents on this and .ak-header__inner), so the DOM stays as it is.
		That row stays pinned, so they are reachable at any scroll position.

		Between 640 and 1400px the table of contents has no entry up here: it is a button of
		its own next to the article (see skin.mustache). Phones keep it in the header — a
		floating square would sit on top of the text there. The label below toggles the same
		checkbox (#ak-toc-toggle in .ak-toc-dock), so it still works without JS; it carries no
		text — the name is the checkbox's aria-label.
	}}
	<div class="ak-local-nav">
		<button type="button" class="ak-local-nav__btn ak-local-nav__menu" id="ak-drawer-toggle" aria-controls="ak-sidebar" aria-expanded="false">
			<svg class="ak-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-menu"/></svg>{{msg-arknights-drawer-toggle}}
		</button>
		{{#toc-enabled}}
		<label class="ak-local-nav__btn ak-local-nav__toc" for="ak-toc-toggle" title="{{msg-toc}}"></label>
		{{/toc-enabled}}
	</div>
</header>
{{!
	The reading preferences panel is on the black header palette like the user menu (upstream
	lists .ak-prefs-panel beside .ak-header in the token remap), but sits outside the header:
	below 1120px the glasses live in the tools card, which closes when the panel opens and would
	hide it along with itself, and a header with backdrop-filter (event themes) would become its
	containing block. Hung from the header's bottom line at ≥ 640px (dialog.show()), centred and modal on phones
	(showModal()) — chrome/prefs.css, client-prefs.js. Its head links to the special page.
}}
{{#data-reading-prefs}}
<dialog class="ak-menu ak-menu--right ak-prefs-panel" id="ak-prefs-panel" aria-labelledby="ak-prefs-panel-title">
	<a class="ak-menu__head" href="{{href}}"><svg class="ak-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-glasses"/></svg><span class="ak-menu__head-name" id="ak-prefs-panel-title">{{msg-label}}</span></a>
	{{#data-form}}{{>ReadingPreferences}}{{/data-form}}
</dialog>
{{/data-reading-prefs}}
